From a18c6bd1e1ce8cd918de100b6d99dd42d474bc8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:31:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] CUDA: group independent rope launches into one kernel

Port of the R9700/HIP track patch 0006 ("CUDA/HIP: group independent rope
launches into one kernel", Claude Fable 5) to the GB10 CUDA track,
unchanged: the code is in the shared ggml-cuda sources and contains no
architecture-gated paths. The Q and K rope of a decoder layer are two
independent launches with the same mode, parameters and position tensor;
the grouped kernel routes each block to its segment and then performs the
stock per-element computation, so the result is byte-identical by
construction.

GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_ROPE_GROUP=1 disables the optimization.

Verified on DGX Spark GB10 (sm_121, CUDA 13.0): greedy text and full float
top-5 logprob hashes match the stock build on 3 prompts.
